<ul>
<li>
<p>When we want to build the left subtree of a node, we look at the part of=
 the inorder array that corresponds to the left subtree. In our example, th=
is is the subarray [2, 9].</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>If this subarray is not empty, we proceed to build the left subtree, sta=
rting with node 9.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>If this subarray is empty, it means there is no left subtree, so the cur=
rent node=E2=80=99s left child is null.</p>
</li>
</ul>
