<p>At each recursive call, once these indexes are obtained, we:</p>
<ol>
<li>
<p>Create the current node using the value pointed at by <code>preorder_ind=
ex</code>.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Increment <code>preorder_index</code> so it points to the value of the n=
ext node to be created.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Make a recursive call to build the current node=E2=80=99s left and right=
 subtrees:</p>
<ul>
<li>Pass in the subarray <code>inorder[0, inorder_index - 1]</code> to buil=
d the left subtree.</li>
<li>Pass in the subarray <code>inorder[inorder_index + 1, n - 1]</code> to =
build the right subtree.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
